IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), s 203 (Part 6, Division 1): sending the financial statements to the members and others entitled, copies on request,
-- the offence of default, and a meeting required after the documents are sent out instead of laid at an annual general meeting.
-- Whether a company need not hold an annual general meeting because of s 175A(1)(a) or (b) is a later wave's: an input named for the fact.
-- s 175A(5), which s 203(5) applies to the notice, is the same later wave's: s 203(5) is encoded as the fact that it applies (NOTES.md, Seams).
-- "Default penalty" is s 408's: the penalty record says that one applies; its amount is not here.

DECLARE `s 203 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 203(1) send the documents to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`
    `s 203(3) furnish the member or debenture holder without charge with a copy of the last financial statements and the auditor's report`
    `s 203(6) convene a meeting for the purpose of laying the documents before the company`

DECLARE `s 203(3A) penalty` HAS
    `s 203(3A) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 203(3A) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 203(3A) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 203(3A) a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 203(7)(a) penalty` HAS
    `s 203(7)(a) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 203(7)(a) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 203(7)(a) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 203(7)(a) a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Section 203(1): sending the documents`

-- src:18826 | 203.—(1) A copy of the financial statements or, in the case of a
-- src:18827 | parent company, a copy of the consolidated financial statements and
-- src:18828 | balance sheet (including every document required by law to be
-- src:18829 | attached thereto), which is duly audited and which (or which but for
-- src:18830 | section 201C) is to be laid before the company in general meeting
-- src:18831 | accompanied by a copy of the auditor’s report thereon must be sent to
-- src:18832 | all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the
-- src:18833 | company —
-- src:18835 | (a) unless subsection (2) applies — not less than 14 days
-- src:18836 | before the date of the meeting; or
-- src:18838 | (b) if the company is not required to hold an annual general
-- src:18839 | meeting because of section 175A(1)(a) — not later than
-- src:18840 | 5 months after the end of the financial year to which the
-- src:18841 | financial statements, or consolidated financial statements
-- src:18842 | and balance sheet, relate.
@ref s 203(1) (src:18826-18842)
GIVEN `the documents are duly audited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents are to be laid before the company in general meeting accompanied by a copy of the auditor's report, or would be but for section 201C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(1) the company must send the documents to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings` MEANS
    IF `the documents are duly audited` AND `the documents are to be laid before the company in general meeting accompanied by a copy of the auditor's report, or would be but for section 201C`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of a copy "which is duly audited and which (or which but for section 201C) is to be laid before the company in general meeting accompanied by a copy of the auditor's report", and a document outside those words is outside the duty (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

@ref s 203(1) (src:18835-18836)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 203(1)(a) the last day for sending the documents` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date of the meeting` 14 Days

@ref s 203(1) (src:18838-18842)
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year to which the documents relate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 203(1)(b) the last day for sending the documents` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the last day of the financial year to which the documents relate` 5 Months

-- Paragraph (a) is "unless subsection (2) applies"; (2) is "if all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company so agree".
-- When (2) applies, the text lets the documents go "less than 14 days before the date of the meeting" and sets no other day: sending on or before the meeting is in time; sending after the meeting is outside the permission and the text is silent.
@ref s 203(1) (src:18826-18842)
GIVEN `the company is not required to hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company agree to the documents being sent less than 14 days before the date of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the financial year to which the documents relate` IS A DATE
      `the day the documents were sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(1) the documents were sent in time` MEANS
    IF `the company is not required to hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)(a)`
    THEN (IF `the day the documents were sent` AT MOST `s 203(1)(b) the last day for sending the documents` `the last day of the financial year to which the documents relate`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the company is not required to hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)(a) — not later than 5 months after the end of the financial year" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    ELSE IF `all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company agree to the documents being sent less than 14 days before the date of the meeting`
         THEN (IF `the day the documents were sent` AT MOST `the date of the meeting`
               THEN JUST TRUE
               ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) permits sending "less than 14 days before the date of the meeting as required under subsection (1)(a)", and a day after the meeting is outside that permission; the text is silent on it
         ELSE (IF `the day the documents were sent` AT MOST `s 203(1)(a) the last day for sending the documents` `the date of the meeting`
               THEN JUST TRUE
               ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) unless subsection (2) applies — not less than 14 days before the date of the meeting" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the "unless" once met is one of the six left to the encoder, NOTES.md fork F-203-unless)

-- The clock counts days from now; the deadline is the number of days until the last day for sending (paragraph (a) or (b)).
@ref s 203(1) (src:18826-18842)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from now until the last day for sending the documents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 203 act`
`s 203(1) the company must send the documents by the last day` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 203(1) send the documents to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`
    WITHIN `the number of days from now until the last day for sending the documents`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send the documents to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings by the last day"

§ `Section 203(2): sending less than 14 days before the meeting`

-- src:18846 | (2) The financial statements, or consolidated financial statements,
-- src:18847 | balance sheet and documents referred to in subsection (1) may be sent
-- src:18848 | less than 14 days before the date of the meeting as required under
-- src:18849 | subsection (1)(a) if all the persons entitled to receive notice of general
-- src:18850 | meetings of the company so agree.
@ref s 203(2) (src:18846-18850)
GIVEN `all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company so agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(2) the documents may be sent less than 14 days before the date of the meeting` MEANS
    IF `all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company so agree`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given "if all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company so agree"; a case outside that is outside the permission and section 203(1)(a) is what then applies (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a function named for a permission whose `if` gate failed)

§ `Section 203(3): a copy on request`

-- src:18854 | (3) Any member of a company (whether or not entitled to have sent
-- src:18855 | to the member copies of the financial statements, or consolidated
-- src:18860 | financial statements and balance sheet) to whom copies have not been
-- src:18861 | sent and any holder of a debenture must, on a request being made by
-- src:18862 | the member or debenture holder to the company, be furnished by the
-- src:18863 | company without charge with a copy of the last financial statements,
-- src:18864 | or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet (including
-- src:18865 | every document required by this Act to be attached thereto) together
-- src:18866 | with a copy of the auditor’s report thereon.
@ref s 203(3) (src:18854-18866)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company to whom copies have not been sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a holder of a debenture of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made a request to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(3) the company must furnish the person without charge with a copy of the last financial statements and the auditor's report` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is a member of the company to whom copies have not been sent` OR `the person is a holder of a debenture of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is owed to "any member of a company ... to whom copies have not been sent and any holder of a debenture", and the subsection is silent on anyone else (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF `the person has made a request to the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, on a request being made by the member or debenture holder to the company, be furnished by the company without charge with a copy" (an "on a request" gate counted as "where": the ruling of 2026-11-05 on delegated definitions, item (c), then the periods ruling, item (b))

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection (the consequence is the offence in subsection (3A)): no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 203(3) (src:18854-18866)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 203 act`
`s 203(3) the company must furnish a copy of the last financial statements on request` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 203(3) furnish the member or debenture holder without charge with a copy of the last financial statements and the auditor's report`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 203(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not furnish the member or debenture holder, without charge, with a copy of the last financial statements" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 203(3A): the offence of default`

-- src:18870 | (3A) If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (3), the
-- src:18871 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall,
-- src:18872 | unless it is proved that the member or holder of a debenture in
-- src:18873 | question has already made a request for and been furnished with a
-- src:18874 | copy of the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements
-- src:18875 | and balance sheet, and all documents referred to in subsection (1) or
-- src:18876 | (3), each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction
-- src:18877 | to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 203(3A) (src:18870-18877)
GIVEN `the member or holder of a debenture in question has already made a request for and been furnished with a copy of the documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(3A) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the member or holder of a debenture in question has already made a request for and been furnished with a copy of the documents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is proved that the member or holder of a debenture in question has already made a request for and been furnished with a copy" (the defence ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b): when it is not proved, "this section gives no defence on these facts")

@ref s 203(3A) (src:18870-18877)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member or holder of a debenture in question has already made a request for and been furnished with a copy of the documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(3A) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (3)`
       AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
       AND (NOT `s 203(3A) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` `the member or holder of a debenture in question has already made a request for and been furnished with a copy of the documents` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (3), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall, unless it is proved that ..., each be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question, fork F-S1 of NOTES.md; the "unless" once met is one of the six left to the encoder, the other reading is NOTHING)

@ref s 203(3A) (src:18870-18877)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member or holder of a debenture in question has already made a request for and been furnished with a copy of the documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 203(3A) penalty`
`s 203(3A) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 203(3A) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (3)` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` `the member or holder of a debenture in question has already made a request for and been furnished with a copy of the documents` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 203(3A) penalty` OF 5000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "an offence" the subsection creates ("a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also ... a default penalty"; the text gives no imprisonment, so the term is 0 months); where the person is not guilty of it the subsection fixes no penalty

§ `Section 203(4) and (4A): requiring a general meeting`

-- src:18881 | (4) In a case referred to in subsection (1)(b), any member or auditor
-- src:18882 | of the company may, by notice to the company not later than 14 days
-- src:18883 | after the day on which the documents referred to in subsection (1)
-- src:18884 | were sent out, require that a general meeting be held for the purpose
-- src:18885 | of laying those documents before the company.
@ref s 203(4) (src:18881-18885)
GIVEN `the day the documents referred to in subsection (1) were sent out` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 203(4) the last day for the notice requiring a general meeting` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the documents referred to in subsection (1) were sent out` 14 Days

-- src:18881 | (4) In a case referred to in subsection (1)(b), any member or auditor
-- src:18882 | of the company may, by notice to the company not later than 14 days
-- src:18883 | after the day on which the documents referred to in subsection (1)
-- src:18884 | were sent out, require that a general meeting be held for the purpose
-- src:18885 | of laying those documents before the company.
@ref s 203(4) (src:18881-18885)
GIVEN `the case is one referred to in subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member or the auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the documents referred to in subsection (1) were sent out` IS A DATE
      `the day the person gives the notice to the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(4) the person may by notice require that a general meeting be held to lay the documents before the company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the case is one referred to in subsection (1)(b)` AND `the person is a member or the auditor of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "any member or auditor of the company" "in a case referred to in subsection (1)(b)", and a case or a person outside those words is outside the grant ("In a case referred to in" is not the word "where"; the grant rule of 2026-11-04, "limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit"; fork F-203-4, NOTES.md)
    ELSE IF `the day the person gives the notice to the company` AT MOST `s 203(4) the last day for the notice requiring a general meeting` `the day the documents referred to in subsection (1) were sent out`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by notice to the company not later than 14 days after the day on which the documents referred to in subsection (1) were sent out" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:18889 | (4A) Where a company is not required to hold an annual general
-- src:18890 | meeting because of section 175A(1)(b), any member or auditor of the
-- src:18891 | company may, by notice to the company not later than 14 days after
-- src:18892 | the day on which the documents referred to in subsection (1) were
-- src:18893 | sent out, require that a general meeting be held for the purpose of
-- src:18894 | laying those documents before the company.
@ref s 203(4A) (src:18889-18894)
GIVEN `the company is not required to hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member or the auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the documents referred to in subsection (1) were sent out` IS A DATE
      `the day the person gives the notice to the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(4A) the person may by notice require that a general meeting be held to lay the documents before the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a member or the auditor of the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "any member or auditor of the company", and the subsection is silent on anyone else (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF NOT `the company is not required to hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)(b)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is not required to hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)(b), any member or auditor of the company may, by notice ..." (a "may" gated by "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3, says do not change it and list it for the maintainer; fork F-203-4A, NOTES.md)
         ELSE (IF `the day the person gives the notice to the company` AT MOST `s 203(4) the last day for the notice requiring a general meeting` `the day the documents referred to in subsection (1) were sent out`
               THEN JUST TRUE
               ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 14 days after the day on which the documents referred to in subsection (1) were sent out" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

§ `Section 203(5): the notice and section 175A(5)`

-- src:18898 | (5) Section 175A(5) applies, with the necessary modifications, to
-- src:18899 | the giving of a notice under subsection (4) or (4A).
@ref s 203(5) (src:18898-18899)
GIVEN `the notice is given under subsection (4) or (4A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(5) section 175A(5) applies, with the necessary modifications, to the giving of the notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice is given under subsection (4) or (4A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "the giving of a notice under subsection (4) or (4A)" and is silent on any other notice; what section 175A(5) then requires is a later wave's

§ `Section 203(6): the directors convene the meeting`

-- src:18903 | (6) The directors of the company must, within 14 days after the date
-- src:18904 | of giving of the notice mentioned in subsection (4) or (4A), convene a
-- src:18905 | meeting for the purpose referred to in that subsection.
@ref s 203(6) (src:18903-18905)
GIVEN `the notice mentioned in subsection (4) or (4A) has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(6) the directors must convene a meeting for the purpose referred to in the notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice mentioned in subsection (4) or (4A) has been given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for "the notice mentioned in subsection (4) or (4A)", and the subsection is silent when no such notice has been given (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

@ref s 203(6) (src:18903-18905)
GIVEN `the date of giving of the notice mentioned in subsection (4) or (4A)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 203(6) the last day for the directors to convene the meeting` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of giving of the notice mentioned in subsection (4) or (4A)` 14 Days

@ref s 203(6) (src:18903-18905)
GIVEN `the date of giving of the notice mentioned in subsection (4) or (4A)` IS A DATE
      `the day the directors convene the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(6) the directors convened the meeting in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the directors convene the meeting` AT MOST `s 203(6) the last day for the directors to convene the meeting` `the date of giving of the notice mentioned in subsection (4) or (4A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 14 days after the date of giving of the notice ..., convene a meeting" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- The clock counts days from the date of giving of the notice; the deadline is 14 days.
@ref s 203(6) (src:18903-18905)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 203 act`
`s 203(6) the directors must within 14 days convene the meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 203(6) convene a meeting for the purpose of laying the documents before the company`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not convene a meeting within 14 days after the date of giving of the notice"

§ `Section 203(7): default in convening the meeting`

-- src:18912 | (7) If default is made in convening the meeting under
-- src:18913 | subsection (6) —
-- src:18915 | (a) each director in default shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:18916 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000;
-- src:18917 | and
-- src:18919 | (b) the Court may, on application of the member or auditor,
-- src:18920 | order a general meeting to be called.
@ref s 203(7) (src:18912-18920)
GIVEN `default is made in convening the meeting under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(7)(a) the person is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in convening the meeting under subsection (6)` AND `the person is a director in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in convening the meeting under subsection (6) — (a) each director in default shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question, fork F-S1 of NOTES.md)

@ref s 203(7) (src:18912-18917)
GIVEN `default is made in convening the meeting under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 203(7)(a) penalty`
`s 203(7)(a) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 203(7)(a) the person is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` `default is made in convening the meeting under subsection (6)` `the person is a director in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 203(7)(a) penalty` OF 5000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "an offence" the paragraph creates ("a fine not exceeding $5,000"; the text gives no imprisonment, so the term is 0 months, and no default penalty); where the person is not guilty of it the paragraph fixes no penalty

@ref s 203(7) (src:18912-18920)
GIVEN `default is made in convening the meeting under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member or auditor who gave the notice has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(7)(b) the Court may order a general meeting to be called` MEANS
    IF NOT `default is made in convening the meeting under subsection (6)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power arises "If default is made in convening the meeting under subsection (6)"; a case outside that is outside the grant (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a function named for a power whose `if` gate failed)
    ELSE IF `the member or auditor who gave the notice has applied to the Court`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court may, on application of the member or auditor, order a general meeting to be called" (a "may" gated by "on application", counted as "upon" under the ruling of 2026-11-05 on delegated definitions, item (c), and so as "where" under the periods ruling, item (b); the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3, says do not change it and list it for the maintainer; fork F-203-7b, NOTES.md)
